DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a = random(2, 4);
$b = random(3, 7);
$c = $a * $b;

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
	[
		[
			'The solution set is \(\big\{\) %s \(\big\}\).  '
				. 'The equation is a conditional equation.'
				. $BR
				. MODES(TeX => '{\color{blue} ', HTML => '<span style="color:DarkBlue">')
				. '(Simplify your answer.  Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)'
				. MODES(TeX => '}', HTML => '</span>'),
			List(0)
		],
		[
			'The solution set is \(\big\{x|x\neq\) %s \(\big\}\).  '
				. 'The equation is an identity.'
				. $BR
				. MODES(TeX => '{\color{blue} ', HTML => '<span style="color:DarkBlue">')
				. '(Simplify your answer.  Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)'
				. MODES(TeX => '}', HTML => '</span>'),
			List(0)
		],
		['The solution set is the set of real numbers.  The equation is an identity.'],
		['The solution set is the empty set.  The equation is inconsistent.']
	],
	2,
	formats => [
		'%1$s.'
			. MODES(HTML => '<div style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;text-align:left">', TeX => '')
			. 'The solution set is {%2$s}.'
			. MODES(HTML => '<br>', TeX => "~~n")
			. 'The equation is a conditional equation.'
			. MODES(HTML => '</div>', TeX => ''),
		'%1$s. '
			. MODES(HTML => '<div style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;text-align:left">', TeX => '')
			. 'The solution set is {x|x &ne; %2$s}.'
			. MODES(HTML => '<br>', TeX => "~~n")
			. 'The equation is an identity.'
			. MODES(HTML => '</div>', TeX => ''),
		'%1$s. '
			. MODES(HTML => '<div style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;text-align:left">', TeX => '')
			. 'The solution set is the set of real numbers.'
			. MODES(HTML => '<br>', TeX => "~~n")
			. 'The equation is an identity.'
			. MODES(HTML => '</div>', TeX => ''),
		'%1$s. '
			. MODES(HTML => '<div style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;text-align:left">', TeX => '')
			. 'The solution set is the empty set.'
			. MODES(HTML => '<br>', TeX => "~~n")
			. 'The equation is inconsistent.'
			. MODES(HTML => '</div>', TeX => '')
	],
	tex_formats => [
		'%1$s.\ {\text{The solution set is }\{%2$s\}.\\'
			. '\text{The equation is a conditional equation.}}',
		'%1$s.\ {\text{The solution set is }\{x|x\neq %2$s\}.\\'
			. '\text{The equation is an identity.}}',
		'%1$s.\ {\text{The solution set is the set of real numbers.}\\'
			. '\text{The equation is an identity.}}',
		'%1$s.\ {\text{The solution set is the empty set.}\\' . '\text{The equation is inconsistent.}}'
	],
	checkTypes => 0
);

Context()->operators->undefine('+', '-', '*', ' *', '* ', '^', '**');

BEGIN_PGML
Solve the following equation.  Then identify the equation as an identity, an inconsistent
equation, or a conditional equation.

>>[`[$a](x - [$b]) = [$a] x - [$c]`]<<

Select the correct choice below, and fill in the answer box if necessary.

[_____]{$rma}
END_PGML

$showHint = 0;
BEGIN_PGML_HINT
Simplify each side of the original equation and then solve for [`x`] if possible.  Note that an
equation that is satisfied by every real number for which both sides are defined is an identity,
and an equation that is satisfied by at least one real number but is not an identity is a
conditional equation.  An inconsistent equation is an equation that has no solution.  Find the
set of values of [`x`] for which the equation is satisfied.
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Distribute [`[$a]`] through the parentheses on the left to obtain

>>[``[$a] x - [$c] = [$a] x - [$c]``]<<

Add [`[@ $a * $b @]`] to both sides to obtain

>>[``[$a]x = [$a]x``]<<

Subtract [`[$a]x`] from both sides to obtain

>>[``0 = 0``]<<

This means that the equation is satisfied for all real numbers, and the equation is an identity.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
